{"tag":"ZFVR","body":"<div class=\"pq-q ue-math\"><p>Fix a finite set <span class=\"m-nb\"><span class=\"katex-lite\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Z\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">Z</span></span></span></span></span>.</span> Let <span class=\"katex-lite\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"X\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span></span></span></span></span> consist of the nonempty subsets of <span class=\"m-nb\"><span class=\"katex-lite\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Z\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">Z</span></span></span></span></span>.</span> Think of <span class=\"katex-lite\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A ∈ X\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7224em;vertical-align:-0.0391em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">∈</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span></span></span></span></span></span> as a menu; the agent picks an item from it at a later date. A preference relation <span class=\"katex-lite\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"≿\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.9592em;vertical-align:-0.2296em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel amsrm\">≿</span></span></span></span></span> is given on <span class=\"m-nb\"><span class=\"katex-lite\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"X\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span></span></span></span></span>.</span> Property 1: whenever <span class=\"katex-lite\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A ≿ B\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.9592em;vertical-align:-0.2296em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel amsrm\">≿</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span></span></span></span></span></span> and <span class=\"katex-lite\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"C\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">C</span></span></span></span></span> meets neither <span class=\"katex-lite\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span></span></span></span></span> nor <span class=\"m-nb\"><span class=\"katex-lite\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"B\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span></span></span></span></span>,</span> we get <span class=\"m-nb\"><span class=\"katex-lite\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A ∪ C ≿ B ∪ C\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.9592em;vertical-align:-0.2296em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">∪</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">C</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel amsrm\">≿</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">∪</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">C</span></span></span></span></span></span>;</span> the same holds for <span class=\"m-nb\"><span class=\"katex-lite\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"≻\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.5782em;vertical-align:-0.0391em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≻</span></span></span></span></span>.</span> Property 2: take <span class=\"m-nb\"><span class=\"katex-lite\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"x ∈ Z\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7224em;vertical-align:-0.0391em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">∈</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">Z</span></span></span></span></span></span>.</span> If <span class=\"katex-lite\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"x ≻ y\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen\">{</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mclose\">}</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≻</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">{</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span><span class=\"mclose\">}</span></span></span></span></span></span> holds for each <span class=\"m-nb\"><span class=\"katex-lite\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"y ∈ A\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8778em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">∈</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span></span></span></span></span></span>,</span> then <span class=\"m-nb\"><span class=\"katex-lite\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A ∪ x ≻ A\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">∪</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">{</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mclose\">}</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≻</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span></span></span></span></span></span>.</span> If instead <span class=\"katex-lite\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"y ≻ x\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen\">{</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span><span class=\"mclose\">}</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≻</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">{</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mclose\">}</span></span></span></span></span></span> holds for each <span class=\"m-nb\"><span class=\"katex-lite\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"y ∈ A\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8778em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">∈</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span></span></span></span></span></span>,</span> then <span class=\"m-nb\"><span class=\"katex-lite\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A ≻ A ∪ x\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≻</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">∪</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">{</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mclose\">}</span></span></span></span></span></span>.</span></p></div><ol class=\"pq-parts\" role=\"list\"><li class=\"pq-part\"><span class=\"pq-l\" aria-label=\"Part (a)\">a</span><div class=\"pq-pq\"><div class=\"ue-math\"><p>How reasonable is each property? Discuss.</p></div><p class=\"pq-none\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><circle cx=\"8\" cy=\"8\" r=\"6.75\"/><path d=\"M5.2 8h5.6\"/></svg>Not a formal statement</p></div></li><li class=\"pq-part\"><span class=\"pq-l\" aria-label=\"Part (b)\">b</span><div class=\"pq-pq\"><div class=\"ue-math\"><p>Find preference relations that (i) meet both properties, (ii) meet Property 1 but fail Property 2, (iii) meet Property 2 but fail Property 1.</p></div><div class=\"pq-ans\" data-answer><p class=\"pq-ans-k\">Answer</p><div class=\"ue-math\"><p>Yes: an example exists (part (b)(i)).</p></div></div></div></li><li class=\"pq-part\"><span class=\"pq-l\" aria-label=\"Part (c)\">c</span><div class=\"pq-pq\"><div class=\"ue-math\"><p>Suppose some <span class=\"katex-lite\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"x, y, z ∈ Z\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8778em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.044em;\">z</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">∈</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">Z</span></span></span></span></span></span> have <span class=\"m-nb\"><span class=\"katex-lite\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"x ≻ y ≻ z\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen\">{</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mclose\">}</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≻</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">{</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span><span class=\"mclose\">}</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≻</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">{</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.044em;\">z</span><span class=\"mclose\">}</span></span></span></span></span></span>.</span> Prove that then no preference relation has both properties.</p></div><div class=\"pq-ans\" data-answer><p class=\"pq-ans-k\">Answer</p><div class=\"ue-math\"><p>Proved: under a strict chain of three singletons, Property 1 and Property 2 cannot both hold. It is a version of the impossibility theorem of Kannai and Peleg (1984).</p></div></div></div></li></ol>"}